WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.150
Gate 6 is the PIV and CAC binding.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.031
Certificate sign-in is
attribute-driven too:

3
00:00:06.031 --> 00:00:10.391
Entra ID matches a field of the
certificate to a field of the account,

4
00:00:10.391 --> 00:00:15.062
so whoever writes that field decides
which certificate signs in as whom.

5
00:00:15.062 --> 00:00:19.724
The binding lives in
certificateUserIds, as prefixed values.

6
00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:22.388
Names and email addresses
are low affinity.

7
00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.842
The key identifier, the public key hash,

8
00:00:24.842 --> 00:00:29.674
and issuer with serial number are high
affinity, because they can't be reused.

9
00:00:29.674 --> 00:00:33.512
That also means a reissued or
renewed card changes the value.

10
00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:35.731
The limits: ten values per user,

11
00:00:35.731 --> 00:00:39.813
each unique in the tenant,
with case-sensitive prefixes.

12
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:45.062
For cloud-only users, a Privileged
Authentication Administrator or Graph writes it.

13
00:00:45.062 --> 00:00:50.365
For synced users, only Entra Connect
can, from altSecurityIdentities in AD,

14
00:00:50.365 --> 00:00:53.787
and Microsoft doesn't
document Cloud Sync for it.

15
00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.980
Treat that AD write path
like an access slot.
